 helps:**\n- Eliminate repeated handshake cost → faster\n- Fewer total connections needed (100 requests share 10-connection pool instead of 100 separate connections)\n- Server resources better used\n- Better throughput under load\n\n**Example:** 1000 requests without pooling = 1000 handshakes. With 10-connection pool = ~10 handshakes. Handshakes are bottleneck. Pooling sidesteps it.\n\nConnection stays open between requests, ready to go. Under heavy load, queries queue for available pooled connection rather than waiting for new handshake each time.","ttft_ms":12393,"type":"result","duration_ms":13518,"uuid":"f0d29e1c-ed6b-490d-89a1-af87a5242684","ttft_stream_ms":816,"time_to_request_ms":118,"first_content_frame_ms":817,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":1149,"cacheReadInputTokens":7864,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006541399999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":933,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-12T05:14:51.381Z"}